id: gospels-at-your-pace
title: Gospels at your pace
version: 1
creator: Day by Word
summary: The four Gospels, Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John, read straight
  through in 60 readings of whole chapters, sized by reading time.
suits: Readers starting a reading habit, or returning to one, who want one
  manageable reading at a sitting and no deadline.
schedule: sequence
behaviors: pace, finish-date
reading-days: 5
coverage: books
canon: protestant
books: MAT, MRK, LUK, JHN
limitations: It reads the Gospels only, in the order they are printed, so
  much that is told in one Gospel is read again in the next. Readings keep
  chapters whole, so their length varies, from about 3 minutes to about 10.
instructions: Read the next reading whenever you read, in any Bible. If you
  miss a day, your next reading waits for you. At five readings a week the
  plan takes twelve weeks.
source: An original plan by Day by Word. Each Gospel is divided into
  readings of one to three whole chapters, as even in reading time as whole
  chapters allow. Reading times are estimated from word counts of the World
  English Bible, a public-domain translation; the plan can be read in any
  translation.
rights: daybyword-original
review: reviewed
